  "narrative": "I assessed all twelve due discovery results using the signed lower-bound rule for outcome_001: accept only if the signed lower bound exceeds 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the registered direction. All twelve comparisons have adequate cell sizes, so diagnostic insufficiency is not driving any decision. Independent validation requests remain exhausted, so these are dataset-specific finite-sample associations only. H325 accepts the new direction-specific feature_010 lowering claim in the high feature_018/high feature_038 quadrant (signed estimate +0.848, lower +0.637). This directly refines H313: H313 remains a rejection of the registered raising direction, while H325 establishes the opposite dataset-specific association in that quadrant. H326 also accepts a strong interaction within high feature_018 (signed estimate +1.177, lower +0.874), indicating that feature_010's contrast is much lower in the feature_038>=0.5 group than in its complement. Together with accepted H308 raising in high feature_018/low feature_038 contexts, this supports genuine modifier-dependent reversal rather than simple attenuation. H327 and H328 accept threshold-robustness variants (lower bounds +0.732 and +0.704), so the lowering pattern is not confined to the most extreme 0.5/0.5 quadrant. These three lowering claims overlap heavily and remain post-hoc, but their large margins make a chance explanation less likely within this dataset. H329 accepts feature_063 lowering in the crossed low-feature_018/high-feature_038 context among feature_027=0 (signed estimate +0.758, lower +0.477), further localizing feature_063 to feature_027=0, feature_038-positive/high, and feature_018-low backgrounds. H190 and H191 also accept feature_063 localization: positive feature_038 interaction and direct lowering within feature_027=0/feature_037=0/feature_002=0 backgrounds (signed estimates +0.593 and +0.556, lower bounds +0.454 and +0.449). H195 is rejected because the registered lowering direction is contradicted by a near-null negative signed estimate (-0.019, lower -0.142). H207 is rejected for feature_010 raising in feature_038>=0.5 overall; its positive point estimate is tiny and the interval crosses zero (signed estimate +0.053, lower -0.131), consistent with strong context-dependent cancellation. H208 accepts feature_010 raising in low feature_038 (signed estimate +0.887, lower +0.783), reinforcing the existing low-feature_038 raising pattern. H282 and H283 are rejected for feature_063 lowering in the feature_040 log-PFS tails among feature_027=0: point estimates exceed the threshold (+0.323 and +0.245), but lower bounds do not (+0.115 and +0.045), so threshold-supported effects are not demonstrated; this is not proof of absence. I reassessed original H313 unchanged as reject because the newly accepted H325 is a separate opposite-direction claim. Critical caveats: the feature_010 reversal was directionally post-hoc after H313 and the feature_063 pattern is highly context-selected; many tests are correlated and overlapping, so multiple-comparison and conditioning risk remains. All accepted conclusions are finite-sample associations among measured predictors and subgroups in this supplied dataset, not causal, mechanistic, biological, or generalizable claims. I do not register further proposals because validation is exhausted and additional subgroup mining would mostly duplicate accepted patterns while increasing multiplicity."
